``` 
```nodeData['output']``` contains my node definition, which has an output of type ```AnyType("*")```. However, it replaces my correct output data with ```AnyType("*")``` and changes the output name to "".

That’s fine, I handle this with ```onConfigure``` and ```onSerialize``` to bypass it, so it’s not really a big issue.

Now, in the UI, I create this node and choose the ```IMAGE``` type. I then connect the output to a ```Preview Image``` node input—so far, no problems.

